module renderer_upscale

# Called by renderer (the core) each frame with the address of its RenderFrame (frame.h): upscale_prepare first of all
# (it may lower the frame's render size), upscale_run in TAA's resolve's place when it upscales.
export bool upscale_prepare(u64 frame)
export void upscale_run(u64 frame)

category Upscaling
# TAA: the Renderer's own anti-aliasing at full resolution. FSR: AMD's upscaler (FSR 4 on Radeon RX 6000 and later,
# FSR 3.1 elsewhere): the scene renders at the quality's resolution and FSR brings it back to the screen's. DLSS:
# NVIDIA's, on GeForce RTX under Windows (Yea's service); FSR wherever DLSS can't run. Where neither can, TAA.
setting choice upscaler TAA TAA FSR DLSS
# The render resolution for an upscaler: Native (100%, the upscaler's own anti-aliasing; DLAA for DLSS), Quality (67%),
# Balanced (59%), Performance (50%), Ultra Performance (33%).
setting choice quality_mode Quality Native Quality Balanced Performance Ultra_Performance
# DLSS's model. Auto: Transformer on GPUs that run FP8 (RTX 40 and later), CNN elsewhere. CNN: NVIDIA's convolutional
# model, cheap on every RTX (about 0.7 ms at 1440p on an RTX 2080). Transformer: NVIDIA's newer model for each mode
# (sharper, steadier detail), affordable with FP8 but two to five times CNN's cost on RTX 20 and 30, where it can cost
# more than rendering at full size saves.
setting choice dlss_model Auto Auto CNN Transformer
# NVIDIA's DLSS files ship with the game only while DLSS is picked.
service dlss when upscaler DLSS
